From: ms178 <19559105+ms178@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 19:46:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] x86 peephole: shared frame-slot stability engine,
 relay/LEA coalescer, RORX machinst; IR: label-counter hygiene + loop-idiom
 hardening

Backend (x86-64 peephole):

- dead_writes.rs: export FrameSlot, parse_frame_slot and
  store_cannot_alias_slot pub(super); add frame_slot_stable_in_range, a
  fail-closed stability oracle for a frame slot over a line range (no
  overlapping write of any writer family -- plain/XMM/RMW stores, string
  ops, atomics, xsave -- unless provably disjoint byte ranges, plus no
  write to the base register). Breaks cached-slot scans on 32-bit
  push/pop whose implicit %esp motion is invisible to the effects
  tables (i686 reuse precision).
- local_patterns.rs: hoist_loop_invariant_gpr_load and
  promote_loop_invariant_fp_load drop their hand-rolled writer scans
  (movq/movl/movb/movw and movsd only) for the shared engine; fixes
  torture execute/20030613-1.c @O1 where an in-loop `movdqu %xmm0` or a
  GPR store clobbered the hoisted/promoted reload. Adds
  loop_entry_is_unique (single-entry-edge proof incl. jump-table and
  inline-asm vetoes), rbp/rsp slot-base pairing for the FP preheader
  store, and %ymm2/%zmm2 alias defenses around the promoted %xmm2.
- relay_and_lea.rs (new): block-local move-relay elimination and LEA
  folding -- eliminate_move_relays, fold_lea_into_load,
  retarget_producer_into_copy, fold_copy_into_lea_base,
  coalesce_copy_into_rmw -- with loop-aware, RET_LIVE-aware deadness
  plus a whole-function textual-uniqueness guard restricted to
  caller-saved sources outside loops (builtin-bitops-1.c: an
  loop-invariant source folded into an in-loop AND corrupts iteration
  2+; callee-saved sources are owed their entry value at every ret).
- machinst: new MachInst::Rorx (BMI2 rorx, three-operand VEX,
  flag-preserving) with alloc scan/rewrite/emit support; isel selects
  Ror(n) -> Ror(width-n) for S32/S64 immediate rotates (SHA-256/ChaCha
  ARX), gated by the CCC_NO_RORX kill switch.
- alu.rs/emit.rs: fused multiply-accumulate staging -- rematerialisable
  GlobalAddr addends stage directly into the target register instead of
  relaying through %rax, with %rax-liveness soundness notes
  (strlen-4.c) and mirrored rorx arms; fused_madd_global_addr_acc test.
- prologue.rs: post-slot REPLAY home-collision veto for cmp_replay /
  fp_select_cmps / demorgan_branch (pr27285 class): liveness snapshot
  taken before slot assignment moves cached_liveness, veto applied
  after webs are final; extends to __builtin_longjmp-class epilogue
  abandonment.

Backend (i686):

- prologue.rs: demand-scanned callee-saved set across inline asm for
  setjmp/longjmp and nonlocal-goto paths; homing values in callee-saved
  registers is refused when a __builtin_longjmp can abandon the
  epilogue (i686_nonlocal_goto_callee_saved,
  setjmp_longjmp_callee_saved regression tests).

IR passes:

- Label-counter hygiene: loop_memset, loop_unroll, outline_switch and
  tail_call_elim now write the module-wide next_label counter ahead of
  every cloned/outlined label; verify.rs gains a label-counter health
  check (every live label < next_label) with tests. Fixes silent CFG
  misrouting from stale counters handing later passes colliding labels.
- Bare-Value pointer-field completeness: aggregate_sroa (mod/split),
  loop_invert, loop_memset, range_check and vectorize replace
  hand-rolled Operand-only user walks with the exhaustive walker over
  pointer-like bare-Value fields (Load/Store ptr, GEP base, Memcpy,
  va_list), so rewrites and pruning can no longer leave stale
  definitions behind.
- loop_idiom: copy-loop recognition extended to single-block self-loop
  Ptr-IV form (*dst++ = *src++), default-on, memmove for Param roots,
  overlap handling for distinct roots; +312-line rewrite/test extension
  and shell harnesses (check_loop_idiom.sh, check_loop_memset.sh).
- loop_memset: trip-count arithmetic tightened for 64-bit IVs and
  stale-label defense; bit_idioms: narrow_width_bits high-bit rule
  fixed with tests.

CI / evidence:

- Codegen gate: chacha20_block workload added to the golden set and
  baseline (largest hot-function oracle gap); steal-fragility paired
  benchmark records, i686 reuse-precision and pr506-audit evidence
  under .github/evidence/.

Regression tests: 11 new files (torture_20030613_1_cpow_hoist,
memset_loop_iv_escape, fused_madd_global_addr_acc,
peephole_rmw_coalesce_loop_source, pr27285_replay_coalesce,
i686/setjmp callee-saved pairs, loop-idiom harnesses).

