Subject: [PATCH 3/4] peephole(x86): audit OF as well as CF for the shlq32
 cross-family fold

The `movl %S32,%D ; shlq $32,%D` -> `shlq $32,%S` fold was audited for CF
only, on the documented argument that "OF/AF-after-shift are undefined in BOTH
spellings". Undefined licences a compiler to CLOBBER a flag, not to OBSERVE it,
and this pass rewrites lccc's own emitted text. Measured natively (x86-64,
2026-09-13):

  src                 unfolded OF   folded OF   diverges
  0x8000000080000000        0             1   YES
  8 more sources            identical in CF/ZF/SF/PF/RESULT

OF after a multi-bit shift is silicon-deterministic and tracks the pre-shift
MSB, so it diverges exactly when the source's bit 63 is set. A following `adox`
consumes OF as its carry-in and returned 0 vs 1 in the two spellings - a wrong
VALUE, not just a wrong flag.

The hole was worse than "OF not credited": OF readers were actively SKIPPED.
`cf_skip_prefix` skips the whole `set`/`cmov`/`j` prefix family, which is where
lccc's own signed-compare `setl`/`setle`/`setg`/`setge` live
(backend/x86/codegen/comparison.rs, i128_ops.rs) - they read SF!=OF, are not
CFG barriers, and were stepped over as flag-irrelevant. `adox` sat in
CF_SKIP_EXACT (correct for CF: silicon shows it neither reads nor writes CF,
while ADCX is the CF consumer and is already in CF_READERS).

Fix: dual-flag liveness in shift_flags_safe_after (renamed from
shift_cf_safe_after). CF and OF are tracked independently; each dies at the
first instruction that overwrites it; a reader of either vetoes only while that
flag is still live; the fold stands when both are dead, or at a call/ret where
flags are undefined anyway. PARTIAL credit continues the scan instead of
falling through to default-deny, because an OF-blind CF writer (`clc`, `stc`,
`sahf`, `bt*` - each measured as preserving OF) settles CF but leaves OF
divergent.

New tables, both silicon-derived with validated controls (a `mov` probe showed
post-flag 1/0 across presets, an `add` probe 0/0, so the harness can tell the
difference):
- OF_READERS: adox(+l/q), the 10 OF-dependent cc names x set/cmov/j, into, the
  whole-RFLAGS readers (pushf*, syscall, sysenter, int*) which must still veto
  on OF once CF is dead, and the BCD group. Enumerated EXACTLY with no suffix
  stripping - a missed reader is unsound, and `setl` stripped of its `l` is
  `set`, which would silently drop the veto. `lahf` is deliberately absent: it
  loads flags bits 7..0 only, so OF (bit 11) is never read.
- OF_CLOBBER_BASE: 37 verified OF writers, matched against the token and the
  token minus ONE trailing size letter (so addq/andnl/popcntl credit their
  base). Stripping is safe on the credit side only: a false credit accepts with
  OF live (unsound), a false negative just costs folds. Excluded on measurement:
  clc/stc/cmc/sahf and bt/bts/btr/btc (CF-only writers), shifts and rotates (OF
  after a multi-bit shift IS the quantity under audit), div/idiv (undefined),
  mulx/pdep/pext/rorx/shlx/shrx/sarx/crc32/not/bswap/lea/xchg (flag-neutral),
  adcx (writes CF, preserves OF), all SSE/AVX (no flags).
- CF_READERS gains adcxl/adcxq: the tables are exact-match, so the suffixed
  spellings GAS emits were falling through to default-deny.

Tests: 5 new, all mutation-verified. Forcing writes_of true and blanking
OF_READERS (i.e. restoring CF-only semantics) fails the three new refusals -
before_setl_signed_compare, before_adoxq_of_consumer,
when_clc_kills_cf_but_not_of - AND the pre-existing
refuses_movl_shlq32_before_unknown_mnemonic, which is the guard proving the
partial-credit continue is sound only because both credit sets are explicit
whitelists (matching one IS the classification). Two positive controls fold:
replacing the OF reader with an OF writer, and clc-then-addl killing both flags.

Output-neutral by measurement, not argument: per-TU asm identity between the
pre-change and post-change binaries over the whole tests/ corpus -
x86-64 -O0/-O2/-O3/-Os 815 identical / 0 differing at every level, i686 -O2
802 identical / 0 differing. The audited shapes do not occur in lccc's own
output today, so this closes the hole at zero codegen cost.

